  "raw": {
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Goucher_Careers/job/Facilities/Utility-Mechanic_R-0000000865-1": {
      "title": "Utility Mechanic",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The Utility Mechanic is responsible for executing tasks to fulfill the diverse need our growing campus environment to include, driver duties to fulfill the needs of FMS Transportation requests, skilled in the technique of fulfilling moving requests, light bulb maintenance, assist with grounds maintenance duties.  Essential Job Functions: A. Performs the duties of driving a Goucher College vehicle, to fulfill the requests by our campus community of the Facilities Management Services transportation department. ·      Independently maintains a level of knowledge regarding the bus/van trip he/she is driving. ·      Responsible for completing a vehicle inspection log on the assigned vehicle to ensure a safe and operational vehicle before every departure.  Inspections are turned in to the supervisor. ·      Responsible for the cleanliness of each vehicle they are assigned on a daily basis, including cleaning out all trash and debris after each use. ·      Follows all college procedures required to inspect and maintain the safety and performance of the vehicle they are assigned each trip. ·      Responsible for the cleanliness of each vehicle they are assigned on a daily basis, including cleaning out all trash and debris after each use. As assigned, inspects designated area of campus buildings for lights that are out and replaces bulbs/lamps accordingly to make repair. ·      Inspects lamp and ballast to determine when the bulb/lamp needs replaced or if the ballast is deficient.  ·      Monitor each building location for bulb/lamp maintenance as scheduled. Perform the duties of fulfilling diverse requests for disassembling, assembling, moving and transporting furniture and various types of office equipment to complete assigned work order. Furniture includes, but is not limited to tables, chairs, desks, beds, dressers, ward robes, boxes, lights, and various types of office equipment and furniture to complete assigned work orders. ·      Responsible for successfully moving office furniture and accessories (i.e. tables, chairs, desks, boxes) as assigned. ·      Responsible for the organization and timeliness of completing the work order. ·      Responsible for moving and transporting all items listed above in a safe manner. ·      Responsible for moving and transporting all items in a way to protect against the damage of the article being moved.   B.   Perform the duties of assisting in the maintenance of the campus grounds including but not limited to trash clean up, removal of debris, limbs, leaves from the grounds, planting of flowers, trees and shrubs, weed removal out of beds, cleaning drains and keeping rain spouts of flat roofs free of debris, athletic field maintenance and snow removal as required. Other Duties as assigned. C.    Must perform all duties in a safe manner, asking for assistance from another employee or supervisor when needed. ·         Required to complete work orders and associated paperwork i.e. (trip form, work orders, vehicle inspection forms etc.) and turn in daily to the work management office. ·         Regularly maintain the cleanliness of the vans and buses inside and outside as assigned. ·         Operate various equipment and power equipment including but not limited to weed eaters, power edgers, power mowers, sprayers, water wheel, field paint machine, snow blower, hand tools, ladders and related landscape equipment as required. Education: Required:  Minimum of a high school diploma or equivalent.: Professional Experience: Required: Approximately 1 year of experience where driving passengers was a primary responsibility. Preferred: 1 year of experience moving furniture in a commercial setting.   The incumbent must obtain a Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) with a passenger endorsement within one year of hire. Starting pay is $21.74 per hour.                          Job Category: Staff Goucher Benefits Information Application Instructions: Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.   Please submit the following application materials (only for external candidates):   Cover Letter    Resume   3 references   Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer   Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.   Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
    },
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Goucher_Careers/job/Goucher-College-Campus/PT-Campus-Safety_R-0000000835": {
      "title": "PT Campus Safety",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description: The Campus Safety Officer serves as the first point of contact for community members and visitors accessing Goucher’s campus. The Campus Safety Officer is responsible for maintaining safety and security on Goucher’s campus, primarily through access control. Employees will be assigned to evening, night, or rotating shifts, including holidays and weekends. They may also be called in for overtime as needed. Officers must be prepared to work outdoors in all weather conditions and be available for duty at all hours to ensure the continuous operation of the agency. Additional responsibilities include managing security at high-profile and campus-wide events, ensuring attendee safety, coordinating with event staff, and monitoring activities. Officers may also be tasked with building watch, overseeing access control, crowd management, and addressing security concerns during events. Essential Job Functions: 30  % A.  Greet and assist guests and visitors entering the campus, providing friendly and informative assistance. Monitor and enforce access control procedures to ensure only authorized personnel and visitors enter the premises. At specified times, log all visitors entering and leaving the campus, accurately recording necessary details. 30  % B.   Maintain a vigilant presence, continuously observing surroundings and promptly addressing any security concerns or breaches. Monitor CCTV systems to oversee campus activities, traffic and identify any suspicious behavior or incidents. 15  % C.   Communicate effectively via radio with security team members and relevant personnel to coordinate responses and share information. Communicate and maintain good relationships with faculty, staff, students, other law enforcement agencies and public officials.  10 % D. Check emails and other communication channels regularly to stay updated on campus events, security alerts, and operational changes. 5 % E.  Prepare and submit detailed reports on incidents, property damage and any security-related matters as required. 5% F. Support student worker program by training and working alongside individuals for events and activities. This position will work Friday and Saturday 11:00 p.m. to 7:00 a.m. (every other weekend) In accordance with Maryland Senate Bill 760 (2023), any individual employed as a security guard or loss prevention personnel must be licensed as a security guard. Employment in this role is contingent upon obtaining and maintaining a valid Maryland Security Guard Certification. Starting Pay: $18.00 per hour 90-Day Pay Increase: Upon successfully completing the 90-day training period, the hourly rate will increase to $19.00 per hour . Job Category: Staff Application Instructions: Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.  Please submit the following application materials (only for external candidates):  Cover Letter   Resume  3 references  Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer  In accordance with Maryland Senate Bill 760 (2023), any individual employed as a security guard or loss prevention personnel must be licensed as a security guard. Employment in this role is contingent upon obtaining and maintaining a valid Maryland Security Guard Certification. Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.  Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
    },
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Goucher_Careers/job/Julia-Rogers/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Neuroscience_R-0000000861": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Neuroscience",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: Open Rank Professor of Neuroscience   Since its founding in 1885, Goucher College has inspired global changemakers as a place of innovation and excellence. As a private, non-profit liberal arts college of approximately 1,000 undergraduate and 500 graduate students, Goucher is dedicated to teaching students to become complex problem-solvers prepared for the jobs of the future. Small class sizes, a rigorous curriculum, and dedicated faculty and staff allow for personalized mentorship of each student. Named one of the most innovative colleges in the country by U.S. News & World Report , Goucher is a leader in global education and was one of the first, and remains one of the only, colleges in the U.S. to provide 100% of its students with the opportunity to study abroad with no additional tuition surcharges.   The Department of Psychology at Goucher College invite applications for a tenure-track position in neuroscience at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor to begin Fall 2027. We invite applicants who share Goucher’s commitment to fostering a vibrant undergraduate learning environment for all students. The position will support the new undergraduate Neuroscience major, which is housed jointly in the Departments of Psychology and Biological Sciences.   Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Neuroscience or a related field by the time of appointment; area of specialty is open (e.g., computational, cognitive, behavioral, systems, sensory). The ideal candidate will show a commitment to undergraduate education and demonstrate evidence of scholarship potential at a small liberal arts college. This research program should be viable without a dedicated wet lab or vertebrate facility. The candidate will be expected to teach 20 credits (the equivalent of five classes) per year, including Research Methods in Neuroscience, an intermediate-level course and an upper-level seminar in their area of expertise, a course that serves the Goucher Commons Curriculum, and rigorous mentoring of undergraduates on a research team. The successful candidate will play a vital role in the Neuroscience program by advising Neuroscience majors and helping to grow the program. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to teaching students from a wide range of backgrounds and a dedication to engaged pedagogies that support student success.   Qualifications:    Required: Ph.D. in Neuroscience or related field at the time of appointment.     Preferred: Ph.D. and Postdoctoral training. Teaching experience and/or professional development at the undergraduate level.     Salary Ranges:   Assistant: $77,727-$86,364 Associate: $89,387-$99,319     Application Instructions:   Applicants are required to submit (1) a curriculum vita, (2) a cover letter, (3) a statement of teaching philosophy which speaks to the applicant’s pedagogical approaches to instruction, classroom practices and strategies, relevant teaching experience, and ability to teach to students from a wide range of backgrounds in a liberal arts college setting, and (4) a statement of research interests. In addition, three (3) confidential letters of recommendation will be requested from finalists. Review of applications will begin October 19, 2026.   Goucher is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeking applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community.    Job Category: Faculty Goucher Benefits Information"
    },
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Goucher_Careers/job/Goucher-College-Campus/Pilates-Instructor-II_R-0000000834-1": {
      "title": "Pilates Instructor II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description: To assist in a first line management capacity, administering policies, procedures, functions, and actitivites of the Pilates Center and to teach Pilates private apparatus lessons, group mat classes, and tower classes. Essential Job Functions: 76 %  A.   Teaches apparatus lessons, mat classes, and tower classes 5 %    B.   Communicates with clients and manages teaching schedule 5 %    C.   Assists with Pilates events on campus such as student classes, alumni events, & demonstrations 4 %    D.   Maintains personal client payment cards 4 %    E.   Assists with registration and filing of health forms 3 %    F.   Cleans apparatus room weekly and notifies Director of any stocking needs 3 %    G.  Organizes and updates private wait list and other postings on staff board Education: Required: Pilates Instructor certification through the Pilates Studio or Romana's Pilates (TPNY).   Annual continuing education (CPE) attendance. Preferred:   Undergraduate or graduate degree in dance. Professional Experience: Required:   Teaching experience as an apprentice or instructor Preferred:   Experience in dance . Job Category: Staff Pay Range: $35.00-$36.75 . Goucher Benefits Information . Application Instructions: Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.   Please submit the following application materials:   Cover Letter    Resume   3 references   Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer   Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.   Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
    },
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Goucher_Careers/job/Goucher-College-Campus/Capital-Project-Manager_R-0000000850": {
      "title": "Capital Project Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The Capital Projects Manager reports directly to the Senior Vice President (SVP) for Finance and Operations and has primary responsibility for ensuring the timely and cost-effective development and completion of all campus capital projects. Essential Job Functions: 45% A. Manage Capital Project Portfolio and Delivery: Provide regular progress reports for all capital projects. Regularly identify and manage project dependencies and critical path activities.  Routinely validate project schedules, monitor project cost controls, resolve coordination issues across the College’s portfolio of projects. Manage the process for reviewing and monitoring project submittals, Requests For Information (RFIs) logs, Architectural / Engineering Clarifications (AECs), and preliminary and final As-Built Drawings for compliance with project requirements. Establish and ensure adherence to policies and procedures for new project management standards. Promote sustainable practices across all project delivery methods. Monitor project deliverables for compliance with project requirements. Review construction drawings and specifications; attend pre-bid and bid opening meetings to discuss principal construction features and requirements relating to means and methods; and inform contractors of requirements concerning easements, rights-of-way, and utility services. Attend and proactively participate in project meetings with contractors, design & engineering professionals, and constituent groups. Guide meeting outcomes and decisions towards alignment with the College’s Campus Master Plan and any fiscal constraints posed by its capital improvement plan. Inform contractors of requirements for construction scheduling, progress reporting, safety measures, wage and hour law observances, labor relations, and payroll records. Assist the SVP in understanding current industry trends or future College space needs, generating recommendations for consideration by senior leadership. Lead management of technical aspects for assigned projects, including major repair and maintenance efforts performed by the College’s Facilities Management Services (FMS) team.   25% B. Lead the development of project scopes, budgets, and schedules.  Manage the design phase for all capital projects, including organizing and supervising competitive selection of architects and other consultants as required. Coordinate consultant and stakeholder meetings and activities to ensure institutional goals and regulatory requirements are met. Manage value engineering and/or scope reduction activities as needed to ensure budget compliance. 15% C. Supervise inspection of construction operations for compliance with design intent and specifications. Interpret plans and specifications and confer with contractor representatives to resolve differences of opinions with the design team. Prepare cost estimates and schedules for all capital projects, including new construction, rehabilitation, infrastructure, energy performance, remodeling, mechanical / electrical / plumbing, fire protection, or general repair projects. Coordinate construction operations with any Baltimore County and/or State of Maryland agencies involved in the renovation and construction of college buildings. 10% D. Oversee and manage design professionals in establishing design guidelines, building programs capable of ensuring academic space requirements are met, and identifying the scope and budget parameters of future capital projects. The selected candidate will also be responsible for providing information needed to support fundraising activities. Education: Required: Bachelor's degree or appropriate certification in Engineering, Construction Management, , Project Management certification, or other relevant field of study. Professional Experience: Required: Ten (10) years of related experience in project management, construction management, and/or program management in the construction or building industry. Experience should include contract negotiations and supervision/oversight of construction activities. Strong knowledge of design, construction, and state and local building codes. Candidate must have a proven ability to work independently and be comfortable as both a team leader and team member. Preferred: Prior Supervisory and leadership experience. Experience working within a campus or academic environment. Experience with contract negotiation. 5% Provide policy and technical recommendations to the SVP as well as supporting departments, contractors, and vendors concerning the construction, renovation, and refurbishment of campus structures. . Job Category: Staff Pay Range: $125,000.00-$148,000.00 . Goucher Benefits Information . Application Instructions: Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.   Please submit the following application materials:   Cover Letter    Resume   3 references   Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer   Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.   Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
    },
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Goucher_Careers/job/Van-Meter-Hall/Director-of-Career-and-Life-Design_R-0000000859": {
      "title": "Director of Career and Life Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The Director leads the college’s efforts to infuse life design and career development perspectives throughout the curriculum and co-curriculum while expanding opportunities for multiple forms of work-based learning. Internally, the Director oversees the day-to-day operations of the Career Education Office while serving as a highly visible partner to faculty and staff throughout the college. Externally, the Director develops and leads an employer relations strategy with the goal of expanding work-based learning opportunities, including but not limited to internships, for all Goucher students.   Essential Job Functions: 30%  A.   Internal Strategy, Outreach, and Programming   Maintain up-to-date knowledge of emerging trends and best practices for enhancing career education offerings and student post-graduation outcomes. Marshall this knowledge to formulate and implement strategies appropriate to Goucher’s institutional profile and culture. Collaborate with faculty and staff throughout the college to incorporate career and life design perspectives into classroom-based teaching and learning; experiential education opportunities (including but not limited to study abroad and community-based learning); co-curricular programs (including but not limited to Athletics, Residence Life, and the Student Government Association); and success and academic advising. Develop and deliver presentations, workshops, and trainings for faculty and staff and curate and share related resources as appropriate. Support the promotion and delivery of the 2-credit course, Introduction to Career and Life Design ; serve as Teaching Assistant or Instructor of Record, as appropriate based on qualifications. Develop and implement assessment strategies to measure program efficacy.   30 %  B.   Employer and Community Relations   In coordination with the AVP for GCCBL and members of the President’s Cabinet and college Board of Trustees, develop and implement an employer outreach strategy to expand work-based learning and post-graduation employment opportunities for Goucher students. Areas of emphasis include but are not limited to local and regional corporations, state and local government agencies, area non-profit organizations, and Goucher alumnae/i. Work with other college units (e.g., Advancement, Athletics) to ensure comprehensive coordination and tracking of employer outreach efforts. Conduct outreach to current and prospective employer partners to ascertain the most desirable knowledge and skills for graduates in different fields. Relay those perspectives to relevant faculty and staff and facilitate direct dialogue, as appropriate, between employers and Goucher faculty and staff. In coordination with college leadership, serve as an external spokesperson for Goucher’s career education and life design efforts before a range of audiences.   30%  C.  Career Education Office Operations   Oversee the effective and efficient delivery of core office functions such as classroom presentations, resume review, and one-on-one career counseling. Oversee the delivery of the college’s internship program – including applications for academic credit, micro-internships, and Goucher Intern Funding – and the continuous improvement of the policies and procedures that govern it.  Oversee the efficient and compliant administration of the Student Employment program and work to strengthen its role in student career exploration and development. Support staff in managing policy questions as needed. Create and manage office budgets. Support the professional development of office staff and assist team members as needed with the prioritization of different tasks. Hold counseling appointments and deliver classroom presentations as needed and appropriate to supplement staffing capacity. undefined 10 % D. Data and Storytelling undefined In collaboration with the Office of Institutional Research and Effectiveness, lead efforts to enhance Goucher’s knowledge rate related to post-graduation outcomes. Recommend and implement strategies including in-house outreach and surveys and third-party services. In coordination with the AVP of GCCBL, develop and implement measures of program impact among current students. Collaborate with the Office of Marketing and Communications and the Division of Enrollment and Student Success to tell the story of Goucher’s work with career and life design and its impact on the student experience and post-graduation outcomes.   Education: Required:  Master’s degree in higher education, business, or another relevant field.  Preferred:  Doctoral degree. Professional Experience: Required:  Five years of experience in higher education, some of which must have involved supervision, and a demonstrated record of building employer and/or community partnerships and overseeing experiential education programs. Preferred:  Seven or more years of experience in higher education and prior leadership of institutional efforts to scale career education, work-based learning, and/or experiential education opportunities. Prior college-level teaching experience will be an asset. . Job Category: Staff Pay Range: $93,000.00-$110,500.00 . Goucher Benefits Information . Application Instructions: Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.   Please submit the following application materials:   Cover Letter    Resume   3 references   Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer   Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.   Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
    },
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Goucher_Careers/job/Goucher-College-Campus/Truck-Driver_R-0000000856-1": {
      "title": "Sanitation Operator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: Responsibilities include operating trucks and motorized equipment to transport trash across the campus and visiting each building daily to remove and deposit trash at the central collection point. Essential Job Functions: 25 %   A.   Operates trucks and other types of motorized equipment such as tractors and carts for the purpose of moving trash from one area of the campus to another. 25 % B.   Responsible for visiting each building daily to remove trash and then depositing said trash at the college central collection point. 25 % C.     Cleans building trash rooms and indoor/outdoor receptacles using hoses and as necessary power equipment and necessary cleaning supplies such as gas or electric powered blowers and gas or electric power washers. 10 % D.    Performs Environmental Services technician tasks from time to time such as sweeping, mopping, wiping, dusting, scrubbing, and vacuuming as necessary and assigned in the support of daily operations. 5 %    E.    Properly cleans and maintains assigned vehicles and equipment by washing, polishing, vacuuming, and inspecting all components i.e. fluid levels. 5 %    F.    Perform snow removal duties as assigned. 5 %    G.   Other duties as assigned. Education: Required: High School Diploma or equivalent. Professional Experience: Required: Valid Class C driver's license and 2 years of experience operating a large vehicle (10,000 lbs. or larger). Preferred: 1 year of experience working as a sanitation operator or other similar experience. Starting salary for this positon is $17.60 per hour. Job Category: Staff Application Instructions: Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.   Please submit the following application materials (only for external candidates):   Cover Letter    Resume   3 references   Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer   Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.   Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
    },
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Goucher_Careers/job/Goucher-College-Campus/GPEP---Adjunct-Lecturer_R-0000000566": {
      "title": "GPEP - Adjunct Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-03-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Founded in 2012, the Goucher Prison Education Partnership (GPEP) is a division of Goucher College operating in two Maryland state prisons, the Maryland Correctional Institution for Women (MCIW) and the Maryland Correctional Institution – Jessup (MCIJ). Each year, around 130 GPEP students enroll in college classes taught by faculty from Goucher and other local colleges and universities. They are held to the rigorous academic standards for which Goucher is known. In addition, we provide college preparatory courses in writing and math. GPEP provides students with tutoring, academic advising, all needed books and materials. GPEP students are American Studies majors and also take electives and the various courses that are part of the Goucher Commons Curriculum. We are always looking for additional qualified faculty to teach both Goucher and college preparatory courses. Application Instruction: Interested candidates should submit the following materials: A curriculum vitae A cover letter that contextualizes the candidate’s teaching interests and identifies courses (from the Goucher catalogue or college preparatory) that the candidate is prepared to teach. Contact information for two professional references. We encourage prospective faculty to consult the Goucher College website for information on the American Studies major and Goucher College curriculum. Interviews and opportunities to teach will be available on a rolling basis based on need and current staffing. Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No visa sponsorship is offered for this position. Salary: $1,200-$1,400 per credit (dependent on OR commensurate with experience) Application Instructions: Please submit the following application materials:   Cover Letter    Resume   Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer   Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.   Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
    }
